description:
Add SieveBackend impl for MemoryBackend in tests/common/mod.rs.

WHAT: The test harness backend for sieve integration tests. Follows exact MdnBackend pattern.

ALGORITHM:
1. Add cfg(feature="sieve") use imports near top of common/mod.rs (alongside existing mdn imports):
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")] use jmap_mail_server::SieveBackend;
2. Add impl block at end of common/mod.rs (after the MdnBackend impl):
   #[cfg(feature = "sieve")]
   impl SieveBackend for MemoryBackend {
     type Error = MemoryError;

     fn get_sieve_blob(&self, _account_id: &Id, blob_id: &Id) -> impl Future<...> + Send {
       // Same pattern as MdnBackend::get_blob_bytes:
       // lock inner, clone blobs.get(blob_id), drop lock, return async move { Ok(bytes) }
       let bytes = self.inner.lock().unwrap().blobs.get(blob_id).cloned();
       async move { Ok(bytes) }
     }

     fn validate_sieve_script(&self, _account_id: &Id, blob_id: &Id) -> impl Future<...> + Send {
       // For the memory backend: fetch the blob bytes, do a trivial check.
       // Valid if bytes exist and content is non-empty UTF-8.
       // If blob missing: return Ok(Some("blob not found"))
       // If not valid UTF-8: return Ok(Some("script is not valid UTF-8"))
       // If empty: return Ok(Some("script must not be empty"))
       // Otherwise: Ok(None) (valid)
       // This is sufficient for the integration tests; a real backend would call a Sieve parser.
       let bytes = self.inner.lock().unwrap().blobs.get(blob_id).cloned();
       async move {
         match bytes {
           None => Ok(Some("blob not found".to_owned())),
           Some(b) => {
             if b.is_empty() { return Ok(Some("script must not be empty".to_owned())); }
             match std::str::from_utf8(&b) {
               Err(_) => Ok(Some("script is not valid UTF-8".to_owned())),
               Ok(_) => Ok(None),
             }
           }
         }
       }
     }
   }
3. Also add MemoryBackend::query_objects<SieveScript> support (query_objects is generic via MailBackend supertrait). The MemoryBackend implements query_objects via a match on O::TYPE_NAME. Add a "SieveScript" arm that:
   - Loads all scripts for the account
   - Applies filter (name substring + isActive exact)
   - Sorts by name (then isActive)
   - Returns QueryResult

DEFENSIVE RULES:
- NEVER hold MutexGuard across .await (same rule as MdnBackend)
- Lock, clone needed data, drop lock, then do async work
- test only: mutex is never poisoned in tests — .unwrap() on lock() is acceptable in tests/

AGENT TEAM: Implementer + Tester (Tester verifies the SieveBackend impl compiles and basic operations work before integration tests run)

TESTS: cargo check --test sieve_integration --features sieve passes; MemoryBackend implements SieveBackend; get_sieve_blob returns bytes for known blob and None for unknown blob; validate_sieve_script returns Ok(None) for non-empty UTF-8 content
